# The environment variables Beacon uses. The server does not load this file or the
# repository-root .env file: export a variable in your shell, or put it in front of
# the command. Never commit a key.
#
# The Ember client reads the first five (EmberClient.from_env in server/beacon/ember/).
# The two EMBER_ settings are read from the process's environment only. The server
# reads the rest when it starts (beacon.ingest.build).

# Meta Model API key for Muse Ember. Read only when REPLAY=0, which also needs
# EMBER_SPENT_BEFORE_USD below.
MODEL_API_KEY=

# 1 answers from recorded Ember responses and makes no API calls, which costs $0.
# It is the default, and tests and CI set it. 0 is only for a deliberate real run.
REPLAY=1

# The most the Ember ledger may hold in live spend, in dollars. A paid call that
# could pass it is refused. 3.00 when unset: the plan's "$3 above the Usage page
# total of Nov 26, 2026", the day the ledger began.
# EMBER_STOP_USD=3.00

# The total spend against the $10 credit that Meta's Usage page
# (https://dev.meta.ai/usage) showed before Beacon's first call, in dollars: every
# model, with no model filter. It has no default: with REPLAY=0 the client is
# refused until this is set, to 0 if that is what the page showed. The stop and
# this together may not pass $9.00 of the $10.00 credit.
# EMBER_SPENT_BEFORE_USD=

# Where runtime data goes: the Ember ledger, trace, and recordings, and later
# SQLite files and downloads. The repository's data/ directory when unset. It must
# be an absolute path, and every process that makes paid calls must use the same
# one: the spending stop is counted in the one ledger file under it.
# BEACON_DATA_DIR=

# The sources to poll for real, as a list of: nws, adsblol, 511, openmhz, notices. Unset, every poller
# runs on the invented mock scenario and nothing asks a real source. Naming any
# source turns the mock scenario off for all of them: the live evidence store holds
# nothing a stand-in produced, so a source that is not named is off.
# BEACON_LIVE_SOURCES=nws,511

# The 511 SF Bay API token (https://511.org/open-data/token). Needed when
# BEACON_LIVE_SOURCES names 511.
# BEACON_511_API_KEY=

# A key of adsb.lol's (https://www.adsb.lol/docs/open-data/api), sent as x-api-key.
# Optional: adsb.lol's API is open to everyone under the Open Database License, and
# with no key it allows an address 500 requests a day, so aircraft are asked for
# every three minutes. Beacon has no OpenSky poller: OpenSky's terms require a
# written license for a running service, which nobody has.
# BEACON_ADSBLOL_API_KEY=

# How many requests a day the key allows, which is not in the key: 1,000 for a key
# asked for with adsb.lol's form, 7,200 for somebody who feeds its network. Only
# with a key. Unset, a key is taken to allow 500, as a key had without an account
# does. The poller asks as often as that allows, never more often than every ten
# seconds, and keeps to it across restarts.
# BEACON_ADSBLOL_REQUESTS_PER_DAY=

# 1 says OpenMHz has given Beacon permission to use its audio. Needed when
# BEACON_LIVE_SOURCES names openmhz, which also needs the talkgroups and the budget
# below, a live Ember (REPLAY=0, MODEL_API_KEY, EMBER_SPENT_BEFORE_USD), and ffmpeg
# and bubblewrap (bwrap) on Linux, on a host that does not hand core dumps to a
# collector (kernel.core_pattern must not begin with | or @). Radio spends the Ember
# credit: every call on the talkgroups is heard by Ember, once.
# BEACON_OPENMHZ_PERMITTED=

# The talkgroups to hear, as a list of OpenMHz's numbers for San Francisco's P25
# system, and the ones among them that carry EMS traffic only. Every call on an EMS
# talkgroup is kept as a "medical response" with its crews and block, and no more.
# BEACON_OPENMHZ_TALKGROUPS=
# BEACON_OPENMHZ_EMS_TALKGROUPS=

# The most, in dollars, that hearing radio may cost over every run. No default.
# BEACON_OPENMHZ_BUDGET_USD=

# Hosts a call's audio may be fetched from besides openmhz.com and its subdomains.
# BEACON_OPENMHZ_MEDIA_HOSTS=

# Text files of the street names and the unit ids a real radio row may name, one to a
# line (Hayes St, E36). A name that is not listed is dropped, and with no file a row
# names none: Beacon does not keep what merely has the shape of a street or a unit.
# BEACON_RADIO_STREETS_FILE=
# BEACON_RADIO_UNITS_FILE=

# The https address of a JSON Feed (https://www.jsonfeed.org/version/1.1/) that lists
# an authority's notices as PDF attachments. Needed when BEACON_LIVE_SOURCES names
# notices, with the budget below and a live Ember (REPLAY=0, MODEL_API_KEY,
# EMBER_SPENT_BEFORE_USD). Notices spend the Ember credit: every document is read by
# Ember, once. Name only a feed whose documents Beacon may relay.
# BEACON_NOTICES_FEED_URL=

# The most, in dollars, that reading notices may cost over every run. No default.
# BEACON_NOTICES_BUDGET_USD=

# Hosts a notice's document may be fetched from besides the feed's own.
# BEACON_NOTICES_HOSTS=

# 0 starts the server without its pollers. Run the pollers in one process only.
# BEACON_INGEST=1

# 0 starts the server without notifications: it takes no subscription and sends no
# push. What an earlier server kept is still deleted when a device asks and when
# its time is over. With 1, the default, and BEACON_VAPID_SUBJECT set, the server
# makes the key it signs a push with the first time it starts, in data/push/ (one
# for the mock store and one for the live store). Keep that directory: a
# subscription takes a push from no other key.
# BEACON_PUSH=1

# Whom a push service may write to about this server: a mailto: or https:// address,
# sent to the push service with every push. Needed for notifications: with none,
# the server sends no notifications and takes no subscription, because a push
# service may refuse a push that names nobody (Mozilla's does).
# BEACON_VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com

# A text file that says where blocks are, which gives an incident heard on real
# radio its point on the map: one block to a line, as
# street,hundred block,latitude,longitude (Hayes St,400,37.7766,-122.4236), with
# lines that begin with # skipped. Read for the live store only; the mock scenario
# has its own. Unset, an incident has a point only when 511 lists a closure on its
# street.
# BEACON_BLOCKS_FILE=

# A text file of the public places and bodies an official notice may name, one to a
# line (Civic Center Plaza). Beacon shows its reading of a notice's words only when
# every word is an ordinary one or a listed name: the streets and units of the radio's
# lists above, and these. Read for the live store only.
# BEACON_PLACES_FILE=

# The most, in dollars, that having incidents' stories made (merge_incident) may
# cost over every run. No default: unset, no story is made on the live store. Needs a
# live Ember (REPLAY=0, MODEL_API_KEY, EMBER_SPENT_BEFORE_USD). The mock store's
# stories are a stand-in's and cost nothing.
# BEACON_STORY_BUDGET_USD=

# The most, in dollars, that investigating taps (investigate_tap) may cost over every
# run. No default: unset, a tap on the live store is stored and its answer says it was
# not investigated. Needs a live Ember (REPLAY=0, MODEL_API_KEY,
# EMBER_SPENT_BEFORE_USD). One tap's calls stop at $0.01. On the mock store a stand-in
# investigates, which costs nothing.
# BEACON_INVESTIGATE_BUDGET_USD=
